From cf5e74af6d8c5e751aa3ea5b74bccbc20ff8ffb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:19:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Shafts of sun in the mist, a sharper picture and far lit
 windows under the new look

The last of the WoW Forever effects, three parts with a switch each.

Volumetric fog. The mist of the day (the hour's, the day's roll, a fog
day, an event, the weather, lookmist) keeps its closed form for how thick
it is, and a low-resolution pass now carves it: along each view ray it
asks the sun-shadow map at a few jittered points how much of the mist the
sun reaches, each stretch weighted by the share of the mist it holds, so
trunks and crowns cut dark lanes and the gaps between them fill with
shafts. The look pass then lights the mist toward the sun only by that
share (a Henyey-Greenstein glow, g 0.6, with a floor so a shaft seen
side-on still reads), over a share of the sky too. The look's lamps and
torches glow in the mist: each one's halo is integrated along the ray in
closed form, so it is smooth at any step count. The jitter settles in a
depth-aware resolve blended with last frame's, reprojected and clamped
to the neighbourhood; the fog is upsampled by depth so it never bleeds
round a silhouette. worldFog 0 draws the analytic mist exactly as before.
worldFogQuality 1/2/3: a sample every 4 px with 6 steps, every 4 with
12 (the default), every 2 with 16. lookfog <0-3> holds the mist's
density at a multiple of the day's, lookfog quality <1-3>, lookfog grade.

A sharper picture. A contrast-adaptive sharpen (after AMD's CAS) at the
head of the look pass, on geometry only: each pixel pushed from its four
neighbours, less where they already span the range (no halos) and less
with distance (35% past 120 yd), where alpha-tested leaves would crawl.
worldSharpen 0-1, default 0.4; looksharpen <0-1> | grade.

Lit windows from afar. As each building loads, its window batches (the
MOMT SIDN ones 1.12 lights at night) are pooled into points, one a
window. From 60 yd out (full by 150, gone by 1500) the nearest 64 on
screen are drawn as a soft warm core and halo over the fog, which the
bloom picks up, hidden behind anything more than 5 yd in front of the
window, dimmed by half the mist between, on the windows' own night track
(20:30-21:30 in, 06:00-07:00 out). lookwindows <0-2>.

worldLook 0 has none of it.

